WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.089 --> 00:00:16.430
Hello, and welcome to Al Dente Creepypasta.

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:19.710
Horror stories cooked to perfection with a
splash of red sauce.

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:23.270
My name is CZ and I will be your server this
episode.

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:28.750
Today’s portion was written to take the
holly and jolly out of the holidays, and replace

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:31.220
them with hate and misery.

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:34.040
This shocking ending will leave you devastated.

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:39.820
Let’s dig right in.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:43.960
For the last couple of years, my wife and
I have hosted a Secret Santa gift exchange

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:45.310
during the holidays.

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:49.219
It’s a fairly new tradition, but we thought
it was nice to put together since us and a

00:00:49.219 --> 00:00:52.579
lot of our friends can’t really afford to
buy gifts for everyone.

00:00:52.579 --> 00:00:56.520
We do it a little bit differently than some
people might be accustomed to.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:01:00.789
Everyone randomly gets a name and has to buy
that person a gift around $50.

00:01:00.789 --> 00:01:05.470
We have one get together where everyone opens
their gifts, but even after the swap, you

00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:07.830
never find out who gave you the gift.

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:10.539
My wife and I agreed that part is important.

00:01:10.539 --> 00:01:15.450
She says that what makes the holiday special
is having good faith in all our friends to

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:17.249
get the person something good.

00:01:17.249 --> 00:01:21.420
In other words, if you’re only buying a
gift in order to get recognition for it, than

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:23.729
the whole idea is kind of cheapened.

00:01:23.729 --> 00:01:24.729
Besides.

00:01:24.729 --> 00:01:25.729
These are our friends.

00:01:25.729 --> 00:01:29.250
If you can’t trust them, then who can you
trust?

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:34.209
Sure, there are exceptions where it’s obvious
who gave the gift; like last year when our

00:01:34.209 --> 00:01:37.919
friends Emily and Alaina, who are married,
ended up getting each other.

00:01:37.919 --> 00:01:43.619
Or… also last year; when Cynthia received
a cheap ice tray as her gift from her recently

00:01:43.619 --> 00:01:45.479
ex-boyfriend, Marc.

00:01:45.479 --> 00:01:50.369
We were optimistic that this year would be
filled with positivity… which it was…

00:01:50.369 --> 00:01:51.759
to a point anyway.

00:01:51.759 --> 00:01:56.239
We have a secret santa app that automatically
emails everyone involved and tells them who

00:01:56.239 --> 00:01:57.239
they got.

00:01:57.239 --> 00:02:01.969
It’s great, because it allows us as the
organizers to not get our Secret Santas spoiled.

00:02:01.969 --> 00:02:04.840
I got Troy, the newest addition to our party
this year.

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:07.840
I think I got the perfect gift for him too.

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:11.350
Every time I go over to his apartment, there’s
stuff everywhere.

00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:13.100
Plates, silverware, Blu-Rays…

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:18.099
It’s not like he’s just too lazy to clean
up after himself, it just seems like he doesn’t

00:02:18.099 --> 00:02:19.750
have anywhere to put it all.

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:23.920
So I got him one of those knife blocks, a
dishrack and a silverware organizer.

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:27.170
That will just cover the kitchen, but it’s
a start.

00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:30.040
I had a feeling Troy was going to appreciate
it.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:32.180
The day of the gift exchange arrived.

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:35.239
We had people drop off gifts in a pile as
they came in.

00:02:35.239 --> 00:02:39.269
We all enjoyed some drinks and snacks as we
caught up with each other for a couple hours

00:02:39.269 --> 00:02:40.989
before getting to down to it.

00:02:40.989 --> 00:02:45.409
By the time we started to open the gifts,
everyone was getting a bit…

00:02:45.409 --> 00:02:46.409
giggly.

00:02:46.409 --> 00:02:50.799
My wife pointed out that Troy seemed to have
taken an interest in her friend Cynthia, which

00:02:50.799 --> 00:02:54.370
we could both get behind since they were the
only two there who were still single.

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:56.760
It seemed like the party was alive and well.

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:00.739
Most of the gifts were really good too, and
people kept up their poker faces as far as

00:03:00.739 --> 00:03:03.349
I could tell when the present they brought
was being opened.

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:08.969
Of course, there were a couple obvious ones,
like our friend James who most likely got

00:03:08.969 --> 00:03:13.079
his own wife, seeing as how she didn’t know
how anyone else would have known what she

00:03:13.079 --> 00:03:14.519
wanted this year.

00:03:14.519 --> 00:03:16.910
Marco actually ended up getting two presents
somehow.

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:18.819
I couldn’t figure out why.

00:03:18.819 --> 00:03:22.829
I was worried that the app had messed up and
someone was going to end up with no presents,

00:03:22.829 --> 00:03:27.079
but I did a quick count and realized there
were 11 total presents for the 10 of us.

00:03:27.079 --> 00:03:31.780
I guess someone just wanted to make Marco’s
day and get him something in addition to buying

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:33.780
something for their person.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:38.459
He ended up loving both presents, so it seemed
like no harm done for the most part, though

00:03:38.459 --> 00:03:41.250
I just worried it was a bit unfair to everyone
else.

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:44.620
The final present remaining came down to my
wife.

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:49.620
It was a little black box wrapped in… what
looked to be just a plastic trash bag and

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:52.040
tied up in actual rope.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:53.040
It was…

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:57.900
I’m not going to lie, a really ugly exterior,
and she had a lot of trouble opening it by

00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:58.900
herself.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:03.050
In fact, nobody could seem to pry the knot
off of it, granted we were all kind of drunk

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:06.409
at that point, so we ended up having to cut
the thing open.

00:04:06.409 --> 00:04:09.969
She opened the box… and pulled out a small
piece of paper.

00:04:09.969 --> 00:04:12.700
She looked upset as she read it.

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:16.670
Then her hands started to shake and her eyes
glazed over.

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:18.530
“What is it?”

00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:20.019
She showed me the slip of paper.

00:04:20.019 --> 00:04:22.079
There were just a couple of words on it.

00:04:22.079 --> 00:04:24.490
“Santa says… you all die.”

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:29.520
I quickly looked inside the box, only to find,
there was nothing else inside.

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:34.220
I can get kind of defensive at times and I
got pretty upset and took it out on everyone.

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:38.080
Within a couple minutes the party was over
and everyone was out in the cold.

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:41.840
I wanted to get to the bottom of who the hell
thought this would be funny by asking everyone

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:45.561
who who their secret santa was and doing a
little research of my own to find out who

00:04:45.561 --> 00:04:50.389
was lying, but she insisted that it wasn’t
that big of a deal and she’d rather not

00:04:50.389 --> 00:04:51.979
ruin it for everyone.

00:04:51.979 --> 00:04:54.780
Still, I felt really betrayed.

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:59.210
These were supposed to be our friends, and
I couldn’t understand who would want to

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:00.460
hurt her like that.

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:04.060
But we were tired and just decided to retire
to bed for the evening.

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:08.319
I told myself I would get her something great
to make up for it and started brainstorming

00:05:08.319 --> 00:05:09.860
some gift ideas.

00:05:09.860 --> 00:05:13.520
But all I could think about was… who would
do this?

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:17.710
I stayed awake for a while longer trying to
think of any reason that someone would have

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:18.800
to try to spook us.

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:21.139
That’s when I heard…

00:05:21.139 --> 00:05:22.831
someone rummaging around the house.

00:05:22.831 --> 00:05:28.919
A chill went up my spine and after being frozen
in fear for a few moments, I sat up and began

00:05:28.919 --> 00:05:30.820
to formulate a plan.

00:05:30.820 --> 00:05:33.430
My wife woke up and asked me what I was doing.

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:35.260
“There’s someone in the house.

00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:38.240
Stay here keep the door locked until I give
you the OK.”

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:41.009
With that, I slipped out and locked the door
behind me.

00:05:41.009 --> 00:05:43.349
My blood was boiling at this point.

00:05:43.349 --> 00:05:47.030
I didn’t know if this had anything to do
with the present from earlier but all I wanted

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:49.919
to do was find who was behind this and bash
his head in.

00:05:49.919 --> 00:05:51.879
The only issue was…

00:05:51.879 --> 00:05:54.129
I couldn’t hear anyone moving around anymore…

00:05:54.129 --> 00:05:57.479
It seemed that the house was quiet.

00:05:57.479 --> 00:06:00.759
I methodically checked the entire upstairs.

00:06:00.759 --> 00:06:01.940
It was empty.

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:05.550
As I was checking the last closet, I heard
a huge crash from downstairs.

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:10.800
I sprinted down, fists blazing, but the scene
I found in the living room was far more horrifying

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:12.050
than I could have imagined.

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:17.770
The tree had been knocked over into the fireplace
which was now on and it had begun to burn.

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:21.460
I heard footsteps running to the door, but
I knew I couldn’t go after him now.

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:25.639
In a panic, I turned off the gas fireplace
and ran to the kitchen to grab a jug of water.

00:06:25.639 --> 00:06:29.250
I poured it over the tree which was beginning
to burn even more, but all I could manage

00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:31.860
to do was slow down the rapidly spreading
fire.

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:36.550
Luckily my wife had already called 9-1-1 and
the fire department showed up before long.

00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:39.030
I was able to slow down the fire enough until
they arrived.

00:06:39.030 --> 00:06:41.310
I wish I could say that was the end of it.

00:06:41.310 --> 00:06:45.400
But it gets worse from there.

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:48.780
The police showed up and questioned us about
what had gone down that evening.

00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:53.850
We told the entire story, and they were particularly
interested in the app we had used to sort

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:55.729
the names for the secret santa.

00:06:55.729 --> 00:06:59.530
The chief told us that an undercover police
officer would be on our block for the time

00:06:59.530 --> 00:07:02.939
being, and to call 9-1-1 if we had any other
disturbances.

00:07:02.939 --> 00:07:07.810
He also gave me a card, a point of contact
for if we had any other information.

00:07:07.810 --> 00:07:12.100
It was nearly 4AM at that point, and we were
ready to put this nightmarish evening behind

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:16.740
us when I got a call from Terry, James’s
wife.

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:20.450
They were both at the secret Santa that night
and I noticed a couple of missed calls from

00:07:20.450 --> 00:07:21.550
from her as well.

00:07:21.550 --> 00:07:25.560
Desperate for more information, I picked up,
but before I could explain the mess that we

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:29.590
had been in, she explained that she was calling
from the hospital.

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:33.569
Apparently they had been driving home from
our house when some maniac ran them off the

00:07:33.569 --> 00:07:34.599
road!

00:07:34.599 --> 00:07:38.711
She was fine, but went on to explain that
James had been injured pretty badly, though

00:07:38.711 --> 00:07:41.040
he was expected to make a recovery.

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:43.370
I decided that enough was enough.

00:07:43.370 --> 00:07:46.330
It was time to do a little investigation of
my own.

00:07:46.330 --> 00:07:50.800
The next morning I headed out to the spot
of the crash, as Terry had described to me.

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:53.830
If I was going to get to the bottom of this,
I had to be thorough.

00:07:53.830 --> 00:07:58.289
Afterall, as far as I knew Terry was trying
to cover up her or James’s guilt with that

00:07:58.289 --> 00:07:59.310
phone call.

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:03.550
I found tire tracks going off the road, but
that really only clears one of them.

00:08:03.550 --> 00:08:05.469
I made a call on over to the hospital.

00:08:05.469 --> 00:08:09.009
I knew they wouldn’t share any information,
since that’s someone’s private medical

00:08:09.009 --> 00:08:13.460
info, but I acted like a concerned family
member and asked if they’d been found.

00:08:13.460 --> 00:08:18.280
I was able to find out they both got admitted
at the same time, so they were both in the

00:08:18.280 --> 00:08:19.280
clear.

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:23.169
My next step was finding out who they got
gifts for in the secret santa, which involved

00:08:23.169 --> 00:08:25.830
me showing up and asking to see the email.

00:08:25.830 --> 00:08:29.639
I had to catch them by surprise to make sure
they didn’t try to doctor anything.

00:08:29.639 --> 00:08:32.810
So I knew I had Troy and my wife had Emily.

00:08:32.810 --> 00:08:37.980
It was already fairly obvious that James had
his wife Terry, but I did find out that Terry

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:38.980
had Alaina.

00:08:38.980 --> 00:08:43.330
Don’t worry about keeping track of all the
names, just know that my list of suspects

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:44.330
was narrowing.

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:48.750
I also discovered that the person who went
after them was in a white van with black tape

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:50.730
over the license plate.

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:52.330
Next on my list were Emily and Alaina.

00:08:52.330 --> 00:08:57.130
It took me a while to come up with an idea
about how I might prove their whereabouts,

00:08:57.130 --> 00:09:00.600
but I ended up finding a way to check on them
without either of them knowing.

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:05.130
See, every year there’s this big Christmas
tree in town square.

00:09:05.130 --> 00:09:08.400
Everyone in the town is encouraged to put
up an ornament of their own, and the whole

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:11.350
thing is livestreamed for the entire month
of December.

00:09:11.350 --> 00:09:14.070
They would most certainly go past it on their
way home.

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:17.600
All I had to do was go back to last night
around the time they should have been driving

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:18.600
home.

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:22.290
Luckily enough, I was able to spot their car
on the stream.

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:26.271
While that didn't necessarily clear both of
them from what happened at our house, it did

00:09:26.271 --> 00:09:29.290
make them innocent of running James and Terry
off the road.

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:33.510
Unless they had just gotten a second car that
I don't know about, but I figured I could

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:36.310
reevaluate them if that came to be the case.

00:09:36.310 --> 00:09:40.500
I also had to make the assumption that the
intruder at our house and the crazy driver

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:45.170
that went after our friends were related incidents,
and the time frame of the events seemed to

00:09:45.170 --> 00:09:46.780
line up with that theory.

00:09:46.780 --> 00:09:50.950
Of course, the nasty present my wife received
only backed this idea up further.

00:09:50.950 --> 00:09:54.940
I tried getting ahold of Emily and Alaina
to see who they got gifts for, but neither

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:56.740
one could be reached.

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:59.920
The next and final couple was Marco and Gina.

00:09:59.920 --> 00:10:04.170
They’d taken an Uber home from the party,
so all I had to do was show up and ask to

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:05.780
see their ride history.

00:10:05.780 --> 00:10:10.070
When I arrived Marco was actually kind of
upset that I was accusing them.

00:10:10.070 --> 00:10:12.261
I thought to myself, this was it.

00:10:12.261 --> 00:10:14.450
It must be one of them.

00:10:14.450 --> 00:10:18.210
But I hadn’t really planned for what I would
do if I’d gotten this far.

00:10:18.210 --> 00:10:20.950
I didn’t bring anything to defend myself
with.

00:10:20.950 --> 00:10:24.140
Not only was Macro a big guy, but it was 2
against one.

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:29.360
I clenched my fists behind my back and slowly
stepped away as Marco yelled at me, going

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:33.720
on about how he was appalled that I didn’t
trust him after everything we’d been through.

00:10:33.720 --> 00:10:36.850
I figured that my best bet was to turn and
run for my car.

00:10:36.850 --> 00:10:39.730
Then I could hopefully make a getaway and
alert the police.

00:10:39.730 --> 00:10:44.280
Tension within me built as I waited for him
to make a move.

00:10:44.280 --> 00:10:48.920
Just when I was ready to turn and run, Gina
came up with the phone to her ear and said

00:10:48.920 --> 00:10:53.020
that Terry was on the line, and she had just
found out about the car crash.

00:10:53.020 --> 00:10:58.520
She invited me in to show me the evidence
I was looking for, and stupidly, I accepted.

00:10:58.520 --> 00:11:02.820
For all I knew, this could have been an act
to lure me in and make me more vulnerable.

00:11:02.820 --> 00:11:08.220
Still, when Gina delivered the news, I thought
I saw something change in Marco’s expression.

00:11:08.220 --> 00:11:10.650
Like an understanding had come over him.

00:11:10.650 --> 00:11:14.580
Like he realized now why I had to see their
whereabouts last night.

00:11:14.580 --> 00:11:18.850
Still I was jumpy inside of their house and
in my mind I was keeping track of where they

00:11:18.850 --> 00:11:23.680
both were at all times for my own safety,
though I tried not to show it.

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:27.690
Marco brought up their trip history on Uber
and… to my surprise, they had gone home

00:11:27.690 --> 00:11:30.110
after the party, no doubt about it.

00:11:30.110 --> 00:11:34.920
They also showed me who their secret santa
recipients were: Marco’s was Cynthia and

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:36.350
Gina’s was James.

00:11:36.350 --> 00:11:40.810
I told them I had to be on my way and headed
out, where a van was pulling up to the curb

00:11:40.810 --> 00:11:41.810
by their house.

00:11:41.810 --> 00:11:45.740
As soon as I looked up at it, it haphazardly
sped away down the street.

00:11:45.740 --> 00:11:50.310
I ran after it and found that the license
plate was covered with black tape, it was

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:52.020
just like what Terry had described to me.

00:11:52.020 --> 00:11:55.040
I dialed 9-1-1 and let them know what had
just happened.

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:58.110
He was still going after people, so I knew
I was racing the clock here.

00:11:58.110 --> 00:12:03.130
There were only two suspects left: Troy and
Cynthia, the two singles who had been flirting

00:12:03.130 --> 00:12:04.130
at the party.

00:12:04.130 --> 00:12:09.570
I hoped to God it wasn’t Troy after I had
put so much into my gift for him, but deep

00:12:09.570 --> 00:12:11.930
down I knew it was.

00:12:11.930 --> 00:12:15.670
The nature of the crime at my house pointed
to it being a male.

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:19.920
Still, I touched base with my wife and told
her to look into Cynthia while I confronted

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:21.000
him.

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:23.420
Everything was boiling down to this.

00:12:23.420 --> 00:12:27.370
Troy lived alone so I wouldn’t be able to
get any info from anyone else.

00:12:27.370 --> 00:12:31.720
He did live in an apartment complex however,
so there had to be a camera somewhere that

00:12:31.720 --> 00:12:34.980
would prove he was out several hours later
after the party ended.

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:39.200
I gave the police chief a call and he agreed
to send someone to meet me at Troy’s apartment

00:12:39.200 --> 00:12:40.590
complex with a warrant.

00:12:40.590 --> 00:12:42.380
I waited out by the office.

00:12:42.380 --> 00:12:44.030
This was our chance to nail him.

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:45.750
What was it taking them so long?

00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:47.040
As I waited around…

00:12:47.040 --> 00:12:49.050
I heard a familiar voice.

00:12:49.050 --> 00:12:50.490
It was Troy.

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:51.500
I was so stupid.

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:54.990
Of course he'd come back here after nearly
getting caught back at Marco’s.

00:12:54.990 --> 00:12:56.850
This was not good.

00:12:56.850 --> 00:12:58.560
He knew I knew.

00:12:58.560 --> 00:13:00.650
But he didn't let onto it right away.

00:13:00.650 --> 00:13:03.340
Well, two can play at that game.

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:05.180
My only choice was to play dumb.

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:07.340
He pretended to be surprised to see me.

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:09.640
He always did have a good poker face.

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:13.640
I told him that I had come to check on him
when I heard about James and Terry.

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:18.130
He told me he had just heard this morning
and went over to the hospital to visit James.

00:13:18.130 --> 00:13:20.240
He was finally telling me something I could
believe.

00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:21.700
A good move on his part.

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:24.370
It would definitely make them less suspicious
of him.

00:13:24.370 --> 00:13:26.330
But that wouldn't work on me.

00:13:26.330 --> 00:13:27.940
I'd caught him red handed.

00:13:27.940 --> 00:13:30.590
But he knew I knew too much.

00:13:30.590 --> 00:13:31.820
What was his plan?

00:13:31.820 --> 00:13:33.800
How long was he going to play dumb?

00:13:33.800 --> 00:13:36.580
All I had to do was stall a little bit longer.

00:13:36.580 --> 00:13:37.990
I decided to press him on it.

00:13:37.990 --> 00:13:42.360
I asked if anything weird had happened after
he had left the night before.

00:13:42.360 --> 00:13:46.320
I was hoping to trip him up with an inconsistency
in his story.

00:13:46.320 --> 00:13:49.430
Something that didn't line up with the actual
timeline of events.

00:13:49.430 --> 00:13:52.870
All I got out of him though, was that he had
gone straight home.

00:13:52.870 --> 00:13:55.850
He asked what I had done after everyone had
left.

00:13:55.850 --> 00:14:00.040
And it was at that moment that something clicked
in my head.

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:02.890
He was going to try paint me as the villain.

00:14:02.890 --> 00:14:07.370
He knew we would be home and asleep after
the party, so we would have no alibi to prove

00:14:07.370 --> 00:14:11.770
that we hadn't gone and run down James’s
car before coming back to set our own Christmas

00:14:11.770 --> 00:14:15.640
tree ablaze in an attempt to make ourselves
look like victims.

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:17.870
After all, we'd setup the party.

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:22.050
We could have structured it so that my wife
would receive the creepy note… from me.

00:14:22.050 --> 00:14:24.400
He was going to try to pin it all on me.

00:14:24.400 --> 00:14:26.770
But I was one step ahead of him.

00:14:26.770 --> 00:14:29.540
The detective arrived.

00:14:29.540 --> 00:14:34.980
I told Troy he was busted, but I knew it would
be a battle to prove my own innocence as well.

00:14:34.980 --> 00:14:36.810
He continued to play dumb.

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:40.920
The detective provided the apartment complex
with a warrant and we all sat down to watch

00:14:40.920 --> 00:14:42.550
the footage.

00:14:42.550 --> 00:14:45.640
This next part, I deeply regret.

00:14:45.640 --> 00:14:50.790
I'll never be able to erase that look of betrayal
out of my mind.

00:14:50.790 --> 00:14:55.660
Because the footage proved that Troy was innocent.

00:14:55.660 --> 00:15:01.620
I wish I had more time to apologise for accusing
him, but I had to go check on my wife.

00:15:01.620 --> 00:15:05.100
All signs now pointed to Cynthia being the
culprit.

00:15:05.100 --> 00:15:09.540
I rushed home where my wife informed me she
had just gotten off the phone with Cynthia’s

00:15:09.540 --> 00:15:10.540
roommate.

00:15:10.540 --> 00:15:12.680
Cynthia was also innocent.

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:14.310
This didn't make any sense.

00:15:14.310 --> 00:15:16.620
We'd cleared everyone who was at the party.

00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:18.010
Had we overlooked someone?

00:15:18.010 --> 00:15:19.820
Was it somebody else?

00:15:19.820 --> 00:15:20.820
Outside of the group?

00:15:20.820 --> 00:15:23.450
We soon got our answer.

00:15:23.450 --> 00:15:27.120
If you're easily disturbed, I suggest you
don't continue.

00:15:27.120 --> 00:15:29.570
We got another call from the police chief.

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:33.680
Emily and Alaina were dead.

00:15:33.680 --> 00:15:38.500
Somebody had broken down their door and slit
both of their throats, leaving them to bleed

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:40.130
out under the Christmas tree.

00:15:40.130 --> 00:15:44.030
The killer had also slathered a message on
the carpet in blood.

00:15:44.030 --> 00:15:49.060
It read, “lesbo freaks” with arrows pointed
up at them.

00:15:49.060 --> 00:15:52.430
I was sickened just by hearing about this.

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:57.280
But the police had a strong lead on who the
killer might be.

00:15:57.280 --> 00:15:58.490
Marc Berklee.

00:15:58.490 --> 00:16:02.200
Cynthia’s ex from last year's secret santa.

00:16:02.200 --> 00:16:06.220
The a-hole who got her an ice tray for a gift.

00:16:06.220 --> 00:16:10.730
Apparently, one of the first things the detective
on our case did was contact the developer

00:16:10.730 --> 00:16:12.380
of the secret santa app.

00:16:12.380 --> 00:16:15.120
He was given a master list of everyone involved.

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:19.470
I guess we never removed Marc from the list
when we added Troy this year and the app told

00:16:19.470 --> 00:16:21.430
Troy to get a present for Marc.

00:16:21.430 --> 00:16:25.600
Troy must have thought it supposed to be Marco,
seeing as how he would have no idea who Marc

00:16:25.600 --> 00:16:26.600
even is.

00:16:26.600 --> 00:16:30.130
That would also explain why Marco ended up
with two gifts.

00:16:30.130 --> 00:16:34.630
Then Marc must have snuck in at some point
and dropped my wife’s gift into the pile.

00:16:34.630 --> 00:16:37.190
It was all starting to come together.

00:16:37.190 --> 00:16:41.670
We also found out that Marc completely lost
his mind when Cynthia had broken up with him

00:16:41.670 --> 00:16:43.370
a little over a year ago.

00:16:43.370 --> 00:16:48.010
There were multiple police reports of him
threatening her, stalking her and loitering

00:16:48.010 --> 00:16:49.540
outside of her apartment.

00:16:49.540 --> 00:16:53.480
Maybe when Marc accidentally got the email
about our secret santa that somehow set him

00:16:53.480 --> 00:16:56.610
off again and he decided to terrorize all
of us.

00:16:56.610 --> 00:16:58.280
Everyone still in her life.

00:16:58.280 --> 00:17:02.160
Everyone who is as close to her as he wishes
he could be.

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:06.250
The chief told me he had already sent his
squad over to Cynthia’s, as Marc would likely

00:17:06.250 --> 00:17:10.260
be heading there next after having hit every
other couple at the party.

00:17:10.260 --> 00:17:12.230
But I knew that wouldn't be the case.

00:17:12.230 --> 00:17:15.510
If Marc really had snuck into my party to
deliver the fake gift, he'd have seen what

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:19.189
went on between Cynthia and Troy and he'd
be in a furious rage.

00:17:19.189 --> 00:17:25.959
He was saving his best, most brutal and cold-blooded
strike for last and Cynthia was never on his

00:17:25.959 --> 00:17:26.959
hit list.

00:17:26.959 --> 00:17:30.879
I raced over to Troy’s as quickly as I could,
but feared I may be too late when I arrived

00:17:30.879 --> 00:17:33.559
to find his front door had been left wide
open.

00:17:33.559 --> 00:17:34.779
I walked inside.

00:17:34.779 --> 00:17:37.549
It seemed…

00:17:37.549 --> 00:17:38.879
strangely empty.

00:17:38.879 --> 00:17:40.730
My heart sank.

00:17:40.730 --> 00:17:42.159
Was I too late?

00:17:42.159 --> 00:17:45.540
Or was Troy even home when Marc had arrived?

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:47.940
I called out.

00:17:47.940 --> 00:17:48.940
“Troy?”

00:17:48.940 --> 00:17:50.340
No response.

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:51.340
“Marc?”

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:55.139
I headed into the kitchen where I saw that
the dish rack and silverware organizer I'd

00:17:55.139 --> 00:17:57.539
gotten him had been put to good use.

00:17:57.539 --> 00:18:00.720
He'd finally tidied his crazy mess of stuff.

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:04.730
For that little moment I was glad I was able
to get him something worthwhile.

00:18:04.730 --> 00:18:06.679
But then it happened.

00:18:06.679 --> 00:18:08.419
I never heard it coming.

00:18:08.419 --> 00:18:14.700
But I did see a shadow come over me as I noticed
the other gift I had gotten Troy.

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:16.220
The knife block.

00:18:16.220 --> 00:18:20.600
But… one of knives was missing.

